  "chapter": {
    "number": 86,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(87) A Psalm of a Song for the sons of Core."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "His foundations are in the holy mountains.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord loves the gates of Sion, more than all the tabernacles of Jacob.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Glorious things have been spoken of you, O city of God. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will make mention of Raab and Babylon to them that know me: behold also the Philistines, and Tyre, and the people of the Ethiopians: these were born there.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A man shall say, Sion is my mother; and such a man was born in her; and the Highest himself has founded her.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord shall recount it in the writing of the people, and of these princes that",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 156
          },
          {
            "text": "were born in her.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The dwelling of all within you is as the dwelling of those that rejoice.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 156,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. have been in her.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 86,
          "verse": 6
        }
      }
    ]
  },
